  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "Both files are in their final intended state.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root causes fixed** (all in the shared parser, so both consumers benefit):\n\n1. **Doubled quotes were rejected.** In `src/state.mjs`, the `afterQuote` branch threw `INVALID_QUOTE` on a second `\"`. It now appends a literal `\"` and returns to `quoted` mode, so `\"\"` unescapes to `\"` — including when the two quotes land in different chunks.\n\n2. **Bare CR was silently accepted.** `pendingCR` was declared but never set; `\\r` was consumed immediately as a record end. Now `\\r` outside quotes sets `pendingCR`, and `src/line.mjs`'s `consumeLine` only finishes the record when the next char is `\\n`; anything else (or EOF, via `finishState`) throws `BARE_CR`. This also makes CRLF split across chunks behave identically to CRLF in one chunk.\n\n3. **Inconsistent line-ending handling between modes.** The `afterQuote` branch now handles `\\r`/`\\n` the same way as the plain branch (finish field, then CRLF-aware record end), so a closing quote followed by a line ending is treated uniformly.\n\n**Unchanged:** `parseRows`/`readItems`/`countItems` exports, `tokenizer.mjs`, `assembler.mjs`, `item-schema.mjs` (`COLUMN_COUNT`/`EMPTY_ID`), `escape.mjs`, and the independent `slug`/`checksum` helpers. Public tests were not modified.\n\n**What I checked:** I traced the state machine by hand against the grammar — CRLF split across chunks, doubled quotes split across chunks, quoted commas/CRLF preserved literally, bare CR mid-input and at EOF, empty input → `[]`, blank line → `['']`, trailing line ending not adding a record, final record without a line ending, `INVALID_QUOTE` for quote-in-unquoted and non-delimiter after closing quote, and `UNTERMINATED_QUOTE` at EOF. I did **not** run any tests (no execution tool available), so I cannot claim the suite passes.",
